age","work_type":"publication","doi":"","openalex_id":"","cited_by_count":0,"quality_score":52,"matched_keywords":[],"author_affiliations":["Apple"],"concepts":[],"official_report":true,"quality_signals":{"company_match_source":"official Apple Machine Learning page https://machinelearning.apple.com/research"},"evidence":[{"source":"official_publication_page","url":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/fine-tuning-strategies","labs":["Apple"],"signals":{"company_match_source":"official Apple Machine Learning page https://machinelearning.apple.com/research"}}],"topic_evidence":{"scope":"ai","classifier_version":2,"method":"official_ai_research_catalogue","ai_research_source":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research","matched_terms":["fine-tuning","self-supervised"],"concept_ids":[],"work_type":"publication"},"ai_research_source":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research"},{"id":"apple:dmv5g5c4if2yg96elbjlcruo","title":"Cross-Domain Data Integration for Entity Disambiguation in Biomedical Text","url":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/cross-domain-data-integration","paper_url":"","alternate_urls":["https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/cross-domain-data-integration"],"alternate_titles":["Cross-Domain Data Integration for Entity Disambiguation in Biomedical Text"],"published":"2021-10-20","authors":["Maya Varma","Laurel Orr","Sen Wu","Megan Leszczynski","Xiao Ling and Christopher Ré"],"abstract":"Named entity disambiguation (NED), which involves mapping textual mentions to structured entities, is particularly challenging in the medical domain due to the presence of rare entities. Existing approaches are limited by the presence of coarse-grained structural resources in biomedical knowledge bases as well as the use of training datasets that provide low coverage over uncommon resources. In this work, we address these issues by proposing a...","companies":["Apple"],"matched_orgs":["Apple"],"company_groups":["company_us"],"company_regions":["US"],"sources":["official_publication_page"],"source":"official_publication_page","work_type":"publication","doi":"","openalex_id":"","cited_by_count":0,"quality_score":52,"matched_keywords":[],"author_affiliations":["Apple"],"concepts":[],"official_report":true,"quality_signals":{"company_match_source":"official Apple Machine Learning page https://machinelearning.apple.com/research"},"evidence":[{"source":"official_publication_page","url":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/cross-domain-data-integration","labs":["Apple"],"signals":{"company_match_source":"official Apple Machine Learning page https://machinelearning.apple.com/research"}}],"topic_evidence":{"scope":"ai","classifier_version":2,"method":"official_ai_research_catalogue","ai_research_source":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research","matched_terms":[],"concept_ids":[],"work_type":"publication"},"ai_research_source":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research"},{"id":"apple:dc0rrgcweqekxuuxzg60tmop","title":"Breiman's Two Cultures: You Don't Have to Choose Sides","url":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/breiman-two-cultures","paper_url":"","alternate_urls":["https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/breiman-two-cultures"],"alternate_titles":["Breiman's Two Cultures: You Don't Have to Choose Sides"],"published":"2021-10-20","authors":["Andrew C. Miller","Nicholas J. Foti","Emily B. Fox"],"abstract":"Breiman's classic paper casts data analysis as a choice between two cultures: data modelers and algorithmic modelers. Stated broadly, data modelers use simple, interpretable models with well-understood theoretical properties to analyze data. Algorithmic modelers prioritize predictive accuracy and use more flexible function approximations to analyze data. This dichotomy overlooks a third set of models—mechanistic models derived from scientific...","companies":["Apple"],"matched_orgs":["Apple"],"company_groups":["company_us"],"company_regions":["US"],"sources":["official_publication_page"],"source":"official_publication_page","work_type":"publication","doi":"","openalex_id":"","cited_by_count":0,"quality_score":52,"matched_keywords":[],"author_affiliations":["Apple"],"concepts":[],"official_report":true,"quality_signals":{"company_match_source":"official Apple Machine Learning page https://machinelearning.apple.com/research"},"evidence":[{"source":"official_publication_page","url":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/breiman-two-cultures","labs":["Apple"],"signals":{"company_match_source":"official Apple Machine Learning page https://machinelearning.apple.com/research"}}],"topic_evidence":{"scope":"ai","classifier_version":2,"method":"official_ai_research_catalogue","ai_research_source":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research","matched_terms":[],"concept_ids":[],"work_type":"publication"},"ai_research_source":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research"},{"id":"apple:ykjhgdw9drasbwyzw4jsaiv4","title":"Finding Experts in Transformer Models","url":"https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/finding-experts","paper_url":"","alternate_urls":["https://machinelearning.apple.com/research/finding-experts"],"alternate_titles":["Finding Experts in Transformer Models"],"published":"2021-10-12","authors":["Xavier Suau","Luca Zappella","Nicholas Apostoloff"],"abstract":"In this work we study the presence of expert units in pre-trained Transformer Models (TM), and how they impact a model's performance. We define expert units to be neurons that are able to classify a concept with a given average precision, where a concept is represented by a binary set of sentences containing the concept (or not). Leveraging the OneSec dataset (Scarlini et al., 2019), we compile a dataset of 1641 concepts that allows diverse...","companies":["Apple"],"matched_orgs":["Apple"],"company_groups":["company_us"],"company_regions":["US"],"sources":["official_publication_page"],"source":"official_publication_page","work_type":"publication","doi":"","openalex_id":"","cited_by_count":0,"qual